# Runtime config — may carry a hoosh bearer token. Commit the *.example files
# (no secrets); keep the real config local. 0.26.0: config lives at
# .thoth/config.cyml (discovered by walking up from CWD, then ~/.thoth);
# ./thoth.cyml is still read as a legacy fallback. .thoth/config.cyml.example
# and .thoth/memory/ stay tracked; only the real .thoth/config.cyml is ignored.
/.thoth/config.cyml
/thoth.cyml
# .thoth/checkpoints/ — the 0.40.0 file-snapshot store behind /rewind. Runtime state, per-machine and
# per-session, and it is written by the test suite too. Never tracked.
# UNANCHORED on purpose (0.43.2): src/checkpoint.cyr builds a CWD-RELATIVE ".thoth/checkpoints/" and
# never resolves the .thoth/ home, so running thoth from a subdirectory writes src/.thoth/checkpoints/
# etc. A root-anchored "/…" rule missed those, and they are verbatim pre-edit copies of source files —
# one `git add .` from being committed, against a comment that promises "never tracked".
# (`/.thoth/config.cyml` above stays anchored: config discovery walks UP, so no subdirectory copy is
# ever created.)
**/.thoth/checkpoints/
